## 17. Core business rules

1. All purchases should be linked to a requisition, except authorized historical or direct-entry records.
2. A requisition must pass its configured approval workflow before purchase.
3. Only assigned purchasers can complete purchases.
4. Requested, approved and actual purchase amounts must remain separate.
5. Each purchased service must be registered in the catalogue.
6. Each individual account must belong to a service/tool.
7. An additional account must not be treated as a new service.
8. Each subscription must have a defined billing cycle.
9. One-time purchases must not generate recurring renewal dates.
10. Previous payment records must be preserved.
11. Renewal dates must be calculated and tracked independently for each subscription.
12. Vendor and direct purchases must be distinguishable.
13. Card visibility must require explicit authorization.
14. Unauthorized users must not retrieve protected card details through reports, exports, APIs or other application screens.
15. Employee information must only support organizational and purchasing workflows.
16. Every important activity must be logged.
17. Changes to approval workflows must not rewrite historical approval records.
18. Expired employee invitations must not create active accounts.

