## 23. Final development guidelines

The development team should follow these principles:

- Build around the purchasing lifecycle, not employee management.
- Avoid duplicating information between requisitions, purchases, accounts and subscriptions.
- Automatically populate account and subscription records from completed purchases wherever possible.
- Keep requested costs, approved costs, actual payments and future renewal costs separate.
- Make approval workflows configurable without requiring code changes.
- Treat payment-card visibility as a separate security boundary.
- Preserve historical records even when employees, services, vendors or cards become inactive.
- Ensure reports reflect actual recorded payments rather than simply adding up subscription prices.
- Design the system to accommodate new tools, categories, vendors and billing cycles.

Final product definition: ESTMS is a centralized internal procurement, subscription, digital asset inventory and expenditure management platform for Riseup Labs. It manages the lifecycle of company software and digital services, from employee requests and approvals through purchasing, payment tracking, account registration, renewals and financial reporting.

Recommended implementation priority: Build the requisition → approval → purchase → account/subscription → reporting workflow first. Implement restricted card visibility as a security requirement from the beginning, not as a feature to add later.

